# Character integrals are finite sums of prescribed disk moments

Theorem statement: `MTT.character_integral_of_disk_moments`
(`434ef507-a279-40f1-8766-9cc2f2ad451a`), by Wenqian, 2026-09-06.

Proof: submission `b7ef57c2-a49a-497c-9279-da50a137452e`, by Wenqian, 2026-09-06 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Let a bounded measure on the p-adic units realize the prescribed signed polynomial disk moments for
an eigenform and its period system. At any positive depth $n$ and critical degree $j$, every
Dirichlet character modulo $p^n$ gives a continuous function $x\mapsto\chi(x)x^j$, whose integral is
the sum of the disk moments multiplied by the corresponding character values over the invertible
residue classes modulo $p^n$. Character values are transported through the specified embedding into
$\mathbf C_p$. Primitivity of the character and ordinarity of the root are not required for this
finite reconstruction.

## Explanation of the source proof

Let a measure on the p-adic units realize the prescribed signed polynomial moments on every residue
disk. For every positive depth, character, and critical degree, its character integral is the finite
sum

$$
\int_{\mathbf Z_p^\times}\chi(x)x^j\,d\mu(x)
=\sum_{a\in(\mathbf Z/p^n\mathbf Z)^\times}
\iota_p(\chi(a))\,M_{s,j}(n,\widetilde a),
$$
where the character on the left is also transported through the specified p-adic embedding, and the
integer representative of a residue class is denoted by a tilde. This identity requires neither
primitivity nor ordinarity.

The invertible residue classes partition the p-adic units. Every integer representative in this
partition is coprime to the prime: it is coprime to the prime power because its residue class is a
unit, and the depth is positive. The moment-realization hypothesis therefore supplies a continuous
function equal to the monomial on that disk and zero outside it, with the prescribed measure value.

Form the finite linear combination of these continuous disk functions with coefficients given by the
character values. At a fixed p-adic unit exactly one summand survives, namely its residue class.
Thus the resulting continuous function is pointwise the character times the monomial. Linearity of
the measure evaluates the finite sum and gives the asserted formula.

